   "text": "I read the structure as a macrocycle built from an N-ethyl indole core, a thiazole, a piperazic acid and a neopentyl ester linker. The SMILES below was written by hand from the drawing and not checked by software.\n\n**Fragments**\n- **Indole:** N1 carries an ethyl group. C2 carries a pyridine ring. C3 carries a CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013CH2\u2013O chain. C5 is bonded to the thiazole.\n- **Pyridine:** it has a 1-methoxyethyl group at the carbon next to the ring N, and a 4-methylpiperazin-1-yl group at the meta position. The methyl on the methoxyethyl carbon is a wedge.\n- **Thiazole:** C4 is bonded to the indole, and C2 carries a CH2 that leads to the amino-acid \u03b1-carbon.\n- **Amino-acid \u03b1-carbon:** it bears an NH acylated by a (fluoromethyl)cyclopropane carbonyl and a C(=O) that links to the piperazic acid N.\n- **Piperazic acid (hexahydropyridazine):** the ring N\u2013N has one N acylated by the \u03b1-carbon C=O and the other N\u2013H next to the ring carbon. That ring carbon bears the hashed ester C(=O)\u2013O\u2013CH2 that closes the macrocycle.\n- **Cyclopropane:** the carbonyl is on a wedge and the CH2F is on a hash.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nI assigned each centre from the wedge and hash bonds and the 2D positions of its neighbours:\n- the methoxyethyl carbon,\n- the \u03b1-carbon,\n- the piperazic carbon,\n- the two cyclopropane carbons.\n\nSMILES: CCn1c(-c2cc(N3CCN(C)CC3)cnc2[C@H](C)OC)c2c3cc(-c4csc(n4)C[C@H](NC(=O)[C@@H]5C[C@H]5CF)C(=O)N6CCC[C@H](N6)C(=O)OCC(C)(C)C2)ccc31"
